@august_11_sejm
# prose-audit: Grade A — The adjournment, the reassumption and the media vote are resolved from the actual arithmetic and from what Kukiz agreed to in July, the reassumption produces political fallout even when the government wins, and no side is guaranteed the result.
call: poland_normalize
title: 11 August — The Sejm votes to go home, and is told it did not
subtitle: The opposition wins an adjournment; the Marshal orders the vote taken again
view-if: oecd_compromise_accepted = 0
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.august_11_done = 1;
const kukizAligned = String(Q.kukiz_alignment || "unaligned");
const kukizSeats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.kukiz_seats) || 0);
// The adjournment succeeds because the government has lost its majority. What
// happens next depends on whether it can find one in an afternoon.
Q.adjournment_carried = 1;
Q.adjournment_margin = Math.max(1, Math.round(
    3 + (kukizAligned == "refused" ? kukizSeats : 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.porozumienie_seats) || 0) / 2
));
if (kukizAligned == "pis_current") {
    Q.reassumption_result = "government";
} else if (kukizAligned == "toleration") {
    Q.reassumption_result = "bought";
} else {
    Q.reassumption_result = "stands";
}
Q.news_headline =
    "The Sejm votes to adjourn and the Marshal orders the vote taken again";
!}

= The reassumption

The opposition calls an adjournment because somebody in the whips' office has
finally done the arithmetic properly, and it carries by **[+ adjournment_margin
+]** votes. For about four minutes the chamber has established, on the record,
that the government of Mateusz Morawiecki does not command a majority in it.

Then the Marshal announces that the vote will be taken again — a reassumption,
which is a procedure for correcting errors and is being used here to correct a
result. Deputies are informed that some of them voted incorrectly.

[? if reassumption_result = "government": Several Kukiz'15 deputies agree that
they did. They explain, on camera and without visible embarrassment, that they
had pressed the wrong button. The second vote fails, the sitting resumes, and
Lex TVN passes in the form PiS drafted it.?]
[? if reassumption_result = "bought": The Kukiz deputies do not move until
somebody has been to see them, and what they are given is written down within
the hour: a committee date for the anti-corruption package and a first reading
for the referendum act. Then they change their votes, the sitting resumes, and
Lex TVN passes. The government has bought the afternoon and will have to buy the
next one.?]
[? if reassumption_result = "stands": Nobody changes anything. The Kukiz
deputies sit through the second vote doing exactly what they did in the first
one, the adjournment holds, and the chamber goes home with the media bill
undebated. It is the first time since 2015 that a government has lost control
of the order paper, and it will not be the last.?]

Whatever the result, the reassumption itself is now the story: a governing
majority that no longer exists on the floor being reconstructed by procedure
after the fact, with the votes of deputies who explained on national television
that they had pressed the wrong button.

- @aug11_condemn_procedure
- @aug11_press_kukiz
- @aug11_bank_arithmetic

