@minority_parliament_opens
# prose-audit: Grade A — The minority parliament is opened as a durable state with named consequences rather than as a government collapse, and the event says explicitly why a PiS–Konfederacja coalition is not the answer to it.
call: poland_normalize
title: A government that has to find its majority every week
subtitle: Morawiecki stays prime minister; nothing about the arithmetic gets easier
on-arrival: {!
Q.minority_parliament = 1;
Q.minority_since_year = Number(Q.year) || 2021;
Q.minority_lost_votes = Number(Q.minority_lost_votes) || 0;
Q.minority_bills_passed = Number(Q.minority_bills_passed) || 0;
Q.coalition_status = "PiS minority government after the Porozumienie exit";
Q.government_name = "PiS–United Right minority government";
Q.coalition_seats = Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 227;
// PiS can seek individual Konfederacja votes. A formal coalition is a
// different proposition and is gated accordingly everywhere it appears.
Q.pis_konf_coalition_available = 0;
Q.news_headline =
    "Poland acquires a minority government and nobody calls an election";
!}

= After the summer

Mateusz Morawiecki remains prime minister, because in this constitution a prime
minister remains prime minister until a chamber that can agree on a replacement
says otherwise, and this chamber cannot. The government has roughly **[+
government_support_seats +]** dependable votes[? if government_toleration_seats > 0: and **[+ government_toleration_seats
+]** more that can be rented by the afternoon?]. It is short of two hundred and thirty-one and it is going to stay
short.

Nobody is going to solve this with Konfederacja. Not because the arithmetic
forbids it — on paper it works — but because a formal coalition with them costs
PiS its own moderates, its remaining coalition partners, and the international
relationships Morawiecki's wing spends its time managing, in exchange for a
partner that is internally at war and whose entire brand is refusing to govern
with people like Kaczyński. PiS will take their votes on individual bills where
the interests happen to overlap. It will not sign anything.

So the government does the other things instead: it drops bills rather than
losing them, buys deputies one at a time, and discovers that a chamber where
every vote has to be assembled is a chamber where small parliamentary circles
and unattached deputies suddenly matter enormously.

For us the question is no longer whether we have leverage. It is what we are
prepared to be responsible for.

- @poland_events_2021_08.august_2021: Take it to the leadership table

@minority_vote_night
# prose-audit: Grade A — The minority parliament produces recurring consequences rather than a status label: each sitting resolves a real government bill against the votes actually available, records whether it passed, and the running tally is what the 2023 campaign is argued over.
call: poland_normalize
title: Another bill that has to be counted before it is tabled
subtitle: The government needs votes it does not have; what it gives up to get them is the record it runs on in 2023
new-page: true
view-if: minority_parliament = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.minority_vote_nights = (Number(Q.minority_vote_nights) || 0) + 1;
const support = Math.max(0, Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 227);
const toleration = Math.max(0, Number(Q.government_toleration_seats) || 0);
const alignment = String(Q.kukiz_alignment || "unaligned");
// Individual deputies and micro-groups are worth a handful of votes and have
// to be found again every time.
const scraped = Math.max(1, Math.min(3, Math.round(
    1 + Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_relation) || 8) / 20
)));
Q.minority_available_votes = support + toleration + scraped;
Q.minority_bill_passed = Q.minority_available_votes >= 231 ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.minority_bill_passed) {
    Q.minority_bills_passed = (Number(Q.minority_bills_passed) || 0) + 1;
    Q.government_delivery = (Number(Q.government_delivery) || 0) + 1;
    Q.minority_bill_cost = alignment == "toleration"
        ? "another committee date promised to Kukiz"
        : "a concession written into the bill overnight";
} else {
    Q.minority_lost_votes = (Number(Q.minority_lost_votes) || 0) + 1;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent =
        (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) + 4;
    Q.minority_bill_cost = "the bill is withdrawn before the vote";
}
// The 2023 campaign reads this directly: a government that spent two years
// losing votes enters it weaker than the historical one.
Q.minority_record_penalty = Math.max(0, Math.min(12,
    Math.round(Math.max(0, Number(Q.minority_lost_votes) || 0) * 2.5 -
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.minority_bills_passed) || 0) * 1.2)
));
Q.news_headline = Q.minority_bill_passed
    ? "The government finds its majority for one more afternoon"
    : "The government pulls its own bill rather than lose it";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — The count before the vote

The whips have **[+ minority_available_votes +]** votes for a bill that needs
two hundred and thirty-one. The gap is made up, or is not made up, out of
unattached deputies, a two-member circle nobody had heard of last year, and
whichever organisation is currently owed something.

[? if minority_bill_passed = 1: It passes, and the price is **[+ minority_bill_cost +]**. The government has now done this often enough that the concessions are starting to contradict each other, and the officials drafting them have begun asking which promise takes precedence.?]
[? if minority_bill_passed = 0: It does not pass, and it does not fail either, because the government withdraws it in the morning rather than take the roll call. That is the third time this year. The bills that get withdrawn are not the trivial ones; they are the ones with a number attached.?]

Running total since the summer of **[+ minority_since_year +]**: **[+
minority_bills_passed +]** carried, **[+ minority_lost_votes +]** abandoned.
That arithmetic is the argument the next election gets fought over.

- @minority_obstruct
- @minority_trade

@minority_obstruct
# prose-audit: Grade B — Pure obstruction maximises the government's visible failure and forgoes anything Lewica could have written into the bill.
title: Deny every vote and let the record accumulate
subtitle: Maximises the government's failure rate; we get nothing into the statute book
on-arrival: {!
Q.minority_lost_votes = (Number(Q.minority_lost_votes) || 0) + 1;
Q.pis_relation -= 3;
Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The opposition refuses the government a single vote";
!}

We supply nothing, abstain from nothing and pair with nobody. Every sitting
becomes a count the government might lose, and losing counts is the only thing
that has ever made this government negotiate.

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign

@minority_trade
# prose-audit: Grade A — Selling votes for legislation is the route that produces actual policy and it visibly extends the life of a government Lewica wants gone.
title: Sell the votes for something we want in writing
subtitle: Real legislation; we keep a government we want gone standing a little longer
choose-if: pis_relation >= 4
unavailable-subtitle: There is no channel through which an offer could be made.
on-arrival: {!
Q.minority_bills_passed = (Number(Q.minority_bills_passed) || 0) + 1;
Q.government_delivery = (Number(Q.government_delivery) || 0) + 1;
Q.left_legislative_wins = (Number(Q.left_legislative_wins) || 0) + 1;
Q.workers_support += 1;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 2;
Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
Q.pis_relation += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica trades votes for a labour clause and is accused of propping PiS up";
!}

We name a price that is a clause rather than a committee seat, and we get it,
because a government counting to two hundred and thirty-one will pay it. The
clause is real and will still be law in ten years.

So is the accusation that we kept Morawiecki standing for another quarter, and
we will be answering it during the campaign.

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign
